  description: `Closes a real, 7-month-continuous write-path leak (product_requirements_v2.integration_operationalization landed/stayed NULL on 1,570 of 4,839 PRD rows, 32.5%, since the column was added 2026-02-02) by adding buildDefaultIntegrationOperationalization() -- a structurally-valid, honestly-empty default (5 canonical keys, each null, derived FROM the gate's own REQUIRED_SUBSECTIONS constant so the two shapes cannot drift) -- and wiring it into all 3 unguarded write paths in scripts/prd/prd-creator.js (INSERT, UPDATE-existing, and the lazy updatePRDWithLLMContent lookup). Also fixes a "fix"->"bugfix" sd_type naming-drift bug that made an authoring-time warning unreachable, exports the gate's emptiness predicate for shared reuse, and teaches the UAT integration-check reader (scripts/modules/uat-assessment/sections/integration-check.js) to treat the all-empty default as NULL-equivalent rather than a false-positive "has content" read. Backfilled all 1,570 live NULL rows in production; 0 of 4,841 rows are NULL as of this retrospective, independently re-verified live.

INCIDENT, the dominant event of this session: the backfill script's first --execute run (scripts/one-off/backfill-integration-operationalization-v2.mjs) wrote \`metadata: { integration_backfill: {...} }\` inside a Supabase .update(). PostgREST PATCH assigns the column VALUE; supabase-js cannot express a jsonb double-pipe merge, and no trigger on product_requirements_v2 merges metadata (SECURITY enumerated and read the source of all 7 non-internal triggers to confirm this). The result was a wholesale column replace, not an additive write: 7,743 metadata keys destroyed across 1,382 of the 1,570 written rows (188 had genuinely empty prior metadata and lost nothing). Destroyed keys included PLAN-phase handoff and sub-agent provenance -- plan_handoff (1,293 rows), database_analysis (312), design_analysis (284), risk_analysis (228), stories_analysis (202), grounding_validation (195), plus parent_orchestrator/parent_sd lineage on 32/26 rows. The incident was independently caught and confirmed, not self-reported: TESTING's EXEC-TO-PLAN pass (evidence 96d51bde, FAIL) and SECURITY's EXEC-TO-PLAN pass (evidence 9d21ac12, FAIL) each independently re-measured the live DB (keyset-paginated full-table reads, a 1,570/1,570-vs-2.1%-base-rate statistical cross-check, and a per-key jsonb_object_keys census against governance_audit_log) and reached the same blast-radius conclusion from different methods, before either had seen the other's findings.

Recovery was possible because governance_audit_trigger (AFTER UPDATE, writes old_values = row_to_json(OLD)) held a complete pre-image of every affected row, with zero contaminating writes since. TESTING's own round-1 finding that "no in-repo recovery path exists" was WRONG (it had probed 5 guessed table names and reasoned from their absence) and was self-corrected in round 2 after enumerating the actual audit tables. Remediation: scripts/one-off/restore-integration-backfill-metadata.mjs restores pre-backfill metadata from governance_audit_log; SECURITY independently re-measured the restore by jsonb containment + value-fidelity checks (not merely "key present") and confirmed 1,364 of 1,382 rows are byte-identical to their pre-incident state with zero over-restore. The final 18 rows (64 keys, all on completed/cancelled SDs, zero active work affected) remain pending human/operator authorization for a second bulk production write, denied 3x by the Claude Code auto-mode permission classifier as of this retrospective -- both SECURITY and TESTING's re-verification passes explicitly recommend NOT gating completion on those 18, since the pre-images are intact and the restore script is idempotent.

Two further defects were found by the same re-verification passes and fixed in follow-up commits: SECURITY's round-2 pass found the restore script's own per-row write guard enforced nothing (it tested only marker presence, which is true of every marked row by definition, not the live single-key invariant its comment claimed) -- a TOCTOU of the exact same defect class inside the remediation script itself, fixed by re-fetching and re-checking each row immediately before writing (commit 413f423c61c). TESTING's round-1 and round-2 passes both found updatePRDWithLLMContent's pre-write SELECT ignored its own error return, so a transient read failure was indistinguishable from "row has no integration_operationalization" and would silently write the placeholder over real authored content -- fixed by checking the error explicitly and leaving the field untouched on a failed read (commit 1f655b36d21). SECURITY also found and fixed a dormant sibling instance of the original blind-replace bug in prd-creator.js's UPDATE-existing branch (armed but never triggered in production, because no caller had yet supplied llmContent.metadata). A follow-up SD (SD-LEO-INFRA-GENERALIZE-ATOMIC-JSONB-001) was filed for the root-cause fix SECURITY named twice: lib/coordinator/safe-metadata-merge.mjs already exists to solve exactly this class of bug, but is hard-scoped to strategic_directives_v2 only, with no equivalent seam for product_requirements_v2 -- deliberately left out of this SD's scope because the generalized helper has 9 live call sites with safety-critical hold-flag semantics that would have blown well past this SD's LOC guidance.`,

